  "description": "Automatic dependency cooldown for every dotnet build: add this package and the build fails when any resolved NuGet package version — direct or transitive — is younger than N days (default 7). Supply-chain protection at build time: malicious package versions are usually detected and removed within days of publication, so builds inside the cooldown window never resolve them. Configurable via MSBuild properties or nuget-cooldown.json (allow lists, custom feeds, warn-only mode); incremental, cached, and CI-friendly with NCD-coded diagnostics. Install with PrivateAssets=all; the standalone CLI is the NuGetCooldown dotnet tool.",
